#* Root environment for the Docker Compose stacks (compose.yaml = production,
#* compose.dev.yaml = staging on the `next` images). Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#* Local development does not use this file - see backend/.env.example and
#* frontend/.env.example.
#*
#* Deploy checklist (production / staging):
#*   1. GitHub: set the Actions variables/secrets listed in README.md (CI) so
#*      the images exist on Docker Hub - the SPA origins are baked into the
#*      frontend image at build time, not read from this file.
#*   2. Fill the "Compose" block below (DOCKERHUB_USERNAME, POSTGRES_*).
#*   3. Append the backend variables from backend/.env.example to this file
#*      and fill them. The backend refuses to boot without: SESSION_SECRET,
#*      TRUST_PROXY, FRONT_WEB_APP_ORIGIN_URL (the public SPA origin),
#*      STRIPE_API_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, a Stripe price id per plan (or
#*      STRIPE_PRICE_ID), BREVO_API_KEY, BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL and the template
#*      ids BREVO_RESET_PASSWORD_TEMPLATE_ID, BREVO_TEAM_INVITE_TEMPLATE_ID and
#*      BREVO_VERIFY_EMAIL_TEMPLATE_ID (create that Brevo template first - an
#*      upgrade without it does not start). PostHog, Telegram and S3 are
#*      optional.
#*      Drop its POSTGRES_* lines (set above - a later empty duplicate would
#*      win). PRISMA_*, PORT and NODE_ENV are overridden by the stacks (the
#*      Prisma URLs point at the database service); keep DEPLOY_ENVIRONMENT
#*      empty (strict production mode).
#*   4. Put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front of the loopback-bound
#*      frontend (8080) and backend (3000) ports.
#*   5. docker compose pull && docker compose up -d --wait
#*      Staging: set NEXT_FRONT_WEB_APP_ORIGIN_URL, then
#*      docker compose -f compose.dev.yaml pull && docker compose -f compose.dev.yaml up -d --wait
#*   6. Never run `prisma db seed` here - the seed creates demo accounts with
#*      a known password and refuses to run outside localhost.
#*
#* Never commit `.env`.

# --- Compose ---
#* Docker Hub namespace CI pushes to (the DOCKERHUB_USERNAME Actions variable)
DOCKERHUB_USERNAME=
#* Image tag to run: `latest` (default) or a pinned `latest-<short sha>` /
#* `latest-<date>` tag for a rollback. Staging uses NEXT_TAG (default `next`)
TAG=latest
NEXT_TAG=next

# --- Database ---
#* Shared by both stacks (each has its own volume). The password is
#* interpolated into the Prisma connection strings - `openssl rand -hex 24`
#* generates a value with no URL-special characters
POSTGRES_DB=saas_template
POSTGRES_USER=saas_template
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# --- Host ports (all bound to 127.0.0.1) ---
#* Production defaults: 8080 / 3000 / 5432; staging: 8081 / 3001 / 5433
FRONTEND_PORT=8080
BACKEND_PORT=3000
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
NEXT_FRONTEND_PORT=8081
NEXT_BACKEND_PORT=3001
NEXT_POSTGRES_PORT=5433

# --- Frontend runtime CSP (both stacks) ---
#* Space-separated extra connect-src origins - the S3 bucket origin
#* (e.g. https://<bucket>.s3.<region>.amazonaws.com) when file uploads are on
NGINX_CSP_CONNECT_EXTRA=
#* Only when VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST is not the EU cloud; empty = image default
NGINX_CSP_POSTHOG_ORIGINS=

# --- Staging (compose.dev.yaml only) ---
#* Overrides FRONT_WEB_APP_ORIGIN_URL for the staging backend - must equal the
#* NEXT_VITE_SITE_BASE_URL Actions variable baked into the `next` bundle
NEXT_FRONT_WEB_APP_ORIGIN_URL=

# --- Backend ---
#* Append the contents of backend/.env.example below this line (step 3).
